{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.TypeBFoldingCpt","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.TypeBFoldingCpt","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFoldingCpt_refutable_on_matter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFoldingCpt_refutable_on_matter","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L305-L315","doc":"**The matter leg is refutable independently**: this caller supplies the *correct*\ndiagram reversal `i ↦ 4 - i`, and an identity crystal action satisfying\n`foldAct_involutive` and `stable_iff_fixed`. It still fails, because an action that moves\nnothing cannot have a non-empty orbit complement — so `anti_iff_moved` carries content that\nthe label fields do not supply.\n\nThis is what separates the repair from a definitional restatement of `ι`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFoldingCpt_refutable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFoldingCpt_refutable","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L297-L303","doc":"**The label leg is refutable**: the identity label map is not the diagram reversal at\n`n = 4`, so it fails `fold_reverses` at `i = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_no_global_chirality_grading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_no_global_chirality_grading","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L269-L290","doc":"**If stable matter exists, the folded crystal carries no globally odd chirality\ngrading.**\n\nIf `stable v` then `foldAct v = v`, so any `chir` with `chir (foldAct w) = !chir w` for all\n`w` gives `chir v = !chir v`, which is false.\n\nThis is the corpus's own obstruction, re-derived from this carrier's fields: compare\n`QOU.StandardModel.Chirality.stable_matter_and_global_chirality_incompatible`, which proves\nthe same dilemma for a bare involution and reads it against this very block. So the\nrepaired carrier is strong enough to entail a known non-trivial result about itself —\nand it agrees with, rather than contradicts, the existing scope-(a) finding that this\nfold involution cannot itself be the chirality involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_stable_iff_not_anti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_stable_iff_not_anti","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L261-L267","doc":"**Matter and antimatter partition the crystal** — the block's word \"complement\", made\nprecise. Derived from the two predicate fields; neither alone gives it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_orbit_eq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_orbit_eq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L251-L259","doc":"**Orbit equality in terms of the carrier's own `fold`.** The transport of\n`typeBFold_orbit_complete_invariant` along `fold_reverses`: two simple roots lie in the\nsame `ι`-orbit exactly when one is the other's fold image. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_label_free_of_odd_strands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_label_free_of_odd_strands","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L235-L249","doc":"**For an odd strand count the fold is fixed-point-free on labels.** The odd-`n` case of\nthe previous; recorded because it is the label-level analogue of the chirality obstruction\nbelow — an odd `n` leaves no `ι`-fixed simple root to carry stable matter.\n\nProved directly from `fold_reverses` rather than by rewriting with the theorem above: the\nlatter's `V`, `foldAct`, `stable` and `anti` are implicit and undetermined by the label\narguments, so the instance search would be stuck on metavariables. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_label_fixed_iff_even_strands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_label_fixed_iff_even_strands","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L224-L233","doc":"**A simple root is `ι`-fixed exactly when `n = 2i`** — so a fixed label exists only for\nan even strand count, and then only at `i = n/2`. The label-level shadow of the block's\nmatter/antimatter split. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_label_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_label_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L214-L222","doc":"**The label fold is an involution** — derived from `fold_reverses` plus the closure of\nthe label range, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TypeBFoldingCpt.anti_iff_moved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TypeBFoldingCpt.anti_iff_moved","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L208-L208","doc":"**Antimatter = the `ι`-orbit complement** — the vertices the fold moves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TypeBFoldingCpt.stable_iff_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TypeBFoldingCpt.stable_iff_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L206-L206","doc":"**Stable matter = fixed points of the folded crystal.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TypeBFoldingCpt.foldAct_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TypeBFoldingCpt.foldAct_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L204-L204","doc":"The fold **induces a `ℤ/2` on the crystal**. This is a genuine assumption: that the\nlabel-level reversal lifts to an involution of crystal vertices at all is part of what\n\"the folded crystal is a symmetric crystal\" asserts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TypeBFoldingCpt.fold_reverses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TypeBFoldingCpt.fold_reverses","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L200-L200","doc":"The fold is the **diagram reversal** `αᵢ ↔ α_{n-i}` on the `A_{n-1}` simple-root\nlabels — the block's own `ι`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TypeBFoldingCpt.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TypeBFoldingCpt.mk","kind":"ctor","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L196-L196","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TypeBFoldingCpt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TypeBFoldingCpt","kind":"class","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L172-L208","doc":"**CONJECTURE (D22).** Type-B Cartan folding realises CPT via symmetric-crystal `ℤ/2`\nfixed points.\n\nThe `𝔰𝔩ₙ` Cartan datum folds under `ι : αᵢ ↔ α_{n-i}`; the induced `ℤ/2` on the folded\nKashiwara crystal splits its vertices into stable matter (the fixed points) and antimatter\n(the orbit complement).\n\n`n` is the strand count, `fold` the label map, `V` the crystal vertex type, `foldAct` the\ninduced involution, and `stable`/`anti` the two predicates. All are supplied by the\n**caller**, so the class is false for data that does not behave this way — see\n`typeBFoldingCpt_refutable` (the label leg) and `typeBFoldingCpt_refutable_on_matter` (the\nphysical leg, which fails independently).\n\nDeliberately **not** stated here: the bar-invariance of GS normal forms (carried by\n`QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction`), the `CPT = C ⊗ P ⊗ T` decomposition, and\nthe identification of the folded datum as type `B` rather than merely rank-`n/2`. See the\nmodule docstring for what must grow first in each case.\n\n**No instance is provided.** Downstream results consume this as\n`[TypeBFoldingCpt n fold foldAct stable anti]` and are genuinely conditional on it.\n\n-- Ref: [kashiwara1991] Kashiwara, \"On crystal bases of the q-analogue of universal enveloping algebras,\" Duke Math. J. 63 (1991)\n-- Ref: [lecouvey2007] Lecouvey, \"Combinatorics of crystal graphs for the root systems of types A_n, B_n, C_n, D_n and G_2,\" MSJ Memoirs 17 (2007)\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:type-b-folding-cpt ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:type-b-folding-cpt","label":"conj:type-b-folding-cpt","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_orbit_complete_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_orbit_complete_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L160-L168","doc":"**`min i (n - i)` is a complete invariant of the `ι`-orbits**: two simple roots share a\nrepresentative exactly when they are equal or swapped by the reversal.\n\nWith `typeBFold_orbit_representative_range`, this says the `ι`-orbits on the `n-1` simple\nroots of `A_{n-1}` are indexed by `[1, n/2]` — i.e. the folded datum has rank `n/2`, which\nis the arithmetic content of the block's `B_{n/2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_orbit_representative_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_orbit_representative_range","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L155-L158","doc":"**Orbit representatives.** `min i (n - i)` is constant on `ι`-orbits and lands in\n`[1, n/2]` — the label set of the folded datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_label_mem_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.typeBFold_label_mem_range","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/type-b-folding-cpt.lean#L151-L153","doc":"The label range `[1, n-1]` is closed under the diagram reversal `i ↦ n - i`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}